  <report name="PierWallFins" title="C006 - Pier Wall, Hairpins and Fin Plates" unit="in" pagesize="816,1056" margin="48,48,48,48" bordermargin="0,0,0,0" collapsemargins="False"><include target="Library.Geometry"/><stylerule type="AnyEquation" name="Required Input" texthighlight="#F7E6B9"/><embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="8"><table name="ProjectStamp" capture="False" colwidths="1:95, 2:165, 3:95, 4:165"><stylerule range="A1:D4" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" vertalign="Center" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.4, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/><row><textcell name="ProjectStampR0C0" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold">Firm</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR0C1" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0">Parsons Transportation Group Inc</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR0C2" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold">Project</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR0C3" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0">I-95 Capacity Improvements from South of SR 152 to South of SR 126</paragraph></textcell></row><row><textcell name="ProjectStampR1C0" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold">Address</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR1C1" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0">1203 Governors Square Blvd, Suite 201, Tallahassee FL 32301</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR1C2" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold">Job no.</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR1C3" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0"/></textcell></row><row><textcell name="ProjectStampR2C0" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold">Designed by</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR2C1" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0">JAT</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR2C2" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold">Date</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR2C3" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0">10/17/2026</paragraph></textcell></row><row><textcell name="ProjectStampR3C0" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold">Checked by</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR3C1" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0">MIK</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR3C2" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold">Date</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="ProjectStampR3C3" capture="False" background="#F1F5FA"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="0"/></textcell></row></table></embed><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="16" spacingafter="2" fontweight="bold">D2 I-95 PEDESTRIAN BRIDGE</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold">C006 - Pier Wall, Hairpins and Fin Plates</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Design basis: AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, 10th edition (2024); FDOT Structures Manual January 2026 (SDG Volume 1, SDM Volume 2)</paragraph><section name="WorkingNotes" capture="False" hide="true"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="4" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#43505C">Working notes (hidden; not part of the submitted calculation): how this edition was produced, its tool status and the open bookkeeping items.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" textcolor="#43505C">Blockpad edition written by calc_common/bpad.py (pier_wall_fins) from the notebook case 82a03356dc83 (package a2bcc233fc8e). Every definition was evaluated independently and compared with the notebook to 1 part in 10⁹.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" textcolor="#43505C">Exported from the notebook for the current case.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" textcolor="#43505C">The calculation was ported from the journal module PierWallFins (journal feb1bb316d08); every definition of the module was evaluated independently from the journal file and reproduced by the notebook to 1 part in 10⁹ before this edition was written.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">A ✓ status covers only the recomputed numerical checks; it is not design acceptance. The equation notes of the calculation are in its report.</paragraph></section><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Inputs are highlighted amber; results are the green tables.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">Overview</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">C006 — Pier Wall, Hairpins and Fin Plates</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Wall reinforcement • selected fin layout • plate resistance • weld-interface actions</paragraph> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True">CALCULATION OVERVIEW</paragraph><table name="C006Box0" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A4" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box0R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">OBJECTIVE / INPUTS / OUTPUT</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box0R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Objective — Size the fin plates for wall gravity and designated hairpin yield force; check distributed wall reinforcement.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box0R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Inputs — Existing wall quantities, pile geometry, concrete/reinforcing properties, and direct-wall wind pressure. Plate layout and local detailing are selected here.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box0R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Output — Selected plate and hairpin arrangement; wall checks; concurrent forces/moments at each fin root for a separate weld calculation.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#A64A20">No weld size, weld throat, electrode, weld resistance, or weld pass/fail is calculated. Local pipe-shell resistance and the atypical hairpin/saddle node require separate completion; a passing plate result does not close those items.</paragraph> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C" fontweight="bold" keepwithnext="True">RESULTS PREVIEW — selected geometry and governing demand family</paragraph><embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="8"><table name="C006Table292" capture="False" colwidths="1:270, 2:270"><stylerule range="A1:B16" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.4, &quot;#6A9075&quot;);"/><stylerule range="A1:B1" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center"/><stylerule range="B2:B16" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center"/><row><textcell name="C006Table292R0C0" capture="False" background="#DCECE0"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">Item</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table292R0C1" capture="False" background="#DCECE0"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">Live result</paragraph></textcell></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R1C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Fin thickness</paragraph></textcell><c formula="t_p to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>1.000 in</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R2C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Fin height</paragraph></textcell><c formula="h_p to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>12.000 in</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R3C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Fin radial projection</paragraph></textcell><c formula="a_p to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>8.000 in</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R4C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Fin count</paragraph></textcell><c formula="n_fin" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>6.000</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R5C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Hairpins per fin</paragraph></textcell><c formula="n_h" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>2.000</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R6C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Hairpin inside bend</paragraph></textcell><c formula="D_s to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>3.750 in</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R7C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Row seat above wall bottom</paragraph></textcell><c formula="z_seat to ft" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>12.000 ft</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R8C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Between-bay fin-force spacing</paragraph></textcell><c formula="L_a to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>32.300 in</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R9C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Across-pile fin-force spacing</paragraph></textcell><c formula="L_b to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>27.700 in</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R10C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Wall end to first force point</paragraph></textcell><c formula="a_o to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>30.350 in</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R11C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Largest plate utilization</paragraph></textcell><c formula="DC_plate" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>0.516</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R12C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Governing actual fin shear</paragraph></textcell><c formula="V_actual to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>41.628 kip</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R13C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Full-yield target shear</paragraph></textcell><c formula="V_target to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>74.458 kip</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R14C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Full-yield target My magnitude</paragraph></textcell><c formula="M_y_target to kip*ft" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>21.718 kip*ft</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table292R15C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">Numerical checks</paragraph></textcell><c formula="Status_numeric" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><textvalue>✓ All Checks Pass</textvalue></c></row></table></embed><section name="C006Strategy01" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006strategy01">1. Geometry and materials</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Import the source wall and pile geometry; define the six-fin upper-row arrangement and local axes.</paragraph> </section><section name="C006Strategy02" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006strategy02">2. Gravity reactions and plate spacing</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Resolve wall gravity at the actual fin-group centers using a symmetric six-support elastic distribution; check equilibrium.</paragraph> </section><section name="C006Strategy03" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006strategy03">3. Hairpins and development</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Check two #5 hairpins per fin, unequal local sharing, full nominal yield target, bends, and available straight development.</paragraph> </section><section name="C006Strategy04" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006strategy04">4. Fin plate resistance</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Check rectangular-bar flexure, lateral-torsional buckling, shear, and an elastic combined-stress screen. No concrete bracing credit.</paragraph> </section><section name="C006Strategy05" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006strategy05">5. Out-of-plane wall strip</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Check a one-foot-high horizontal strip for wind flexure, shear, and service behavior; take reactions into pile contact regions.</paragraph> </section><section name="C006Strategy06" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006strategy06">6. Distributed reinforcement and detailing</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Check shrinkage/temperature, applicable strut-region minimum grids, cover, spacing, development, joints, and mass-concrete screen.</paragraph> </section><section name="C006Strategy07" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006strategy07">7. Weld and pile interface actions</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Export complete concurrent root force/moment sets, distinguish actual load combinations from the hairpin-yield target, and state open interface checks.</paragraph> </section><section name="C006Strategy08" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006strategy08">8. Design summary and verification boundaries</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Collect live checks and selected dimensions; keep unresolved local mechanisms separate from completed checks.</paragraph> </section><table name="C006Box2" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A6" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box2R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">DESIGN BASIS QUICK REFERENCE</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box2R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">RFQ IV.B.2 controls the adopted edition. Basis retained for this module: LRFD 10th Edition (2024), FDOT Structures Manual (January 2026), and project amendments. No newer ACI edition is substituted.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box2R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">LRFD 5.6.3, 5.6.7, 5.7, 5.10.2, 5.10.3, 5.10.6 and 5.10.8: distributed RC wall checks. FDOT SDG 1.4.2, 1.4.4 and 3.10 modify the cover, durability and service-detailing basis.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box2R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">LRFD 5.8.2.4 and 5.13: hanger/anchorage basis. The fully embedded fin is not treated as a prequalified ACI base-plate shear lug. The adopted hanger reduction factor is conservatively lower than the verified LRFD reinforced-concrete STM tie factor.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box2R4" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">LRFD 6.5.4.2, 6.12.2.2.7 and 6.13.5.3: rectangular fin-plate resistance. The additional elastic combined-stress limit is a deliberately conservative project screen, not a quoted LRFD interaction equation.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box2R5" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Fin geometry, one-row layout, elastic reaction model, nominal-yield development target, and tolerances are declared design assumptions. Approval of the complete local hanger/concrete/saddle/pipe mechanism remains a release condition.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <table name="C006Box3" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A6" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box3R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">LOAD PATH AND SCOPE</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box3R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Bridge gravity is not assigned to this wall. Wall gravity passes through its reinforced collection regions, hairpins and bearing saddles into the fin plates and piles. No bond or friction between the pipe and wall is credited for vertical resistance.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box3R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Out-of-plane wind is assigned to concrete-to-pipe contact distributed over the wall height, not concentrated at the upper fin row. Fin out-of-plane loading from forced compatibility is not silently included as zero measured demand.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box3R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The source wall is conservatively weighed gross, without subtracting pipe volumes. The source weight, cap dimensions, pile layout, existing FBMP loads and unrelated calculations are not changed.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box3R4" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The six-support solution is an elastic demand-distribution model, not proof of gravity load collection in the deep wall. Local strut/node design, hanger-to-wall load collection and imposed pile movement remain explicit completion items.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box3R5" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Fin plates are checked for their actual factored reaction and the full nominal yield of their designated two-hairpin group. Nominal yield is not multiplied by the DC load factor and is not claimed to represent actual simultaneous yielding in all fins.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <section name="C006Work01" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006work01">Step 1. Geometry and materials</paragraph></section><embed spacingbefore="4" spacingafter="5"><canvas name="C006FinPlan" title="Selected plan arrangement and force points" unit="in" size="6.5 in; 3.0 in; scaletofit">
                <include target="Library.Geometry"/>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15,2.78,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>SELECTED PLAN ARRANGEMENT AND FORCE POINTS</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15,0.07,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#65717A"><textvalue>NOT TO SCALE — force signs follow the defined local axes.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="0.4,0.6,0; 6.1,0.6,0; 6.1,1.7,0; 0.4,1.7,0; 0.4,0.6,0" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.8"/>
                <circle center="1.0,1.15,0" normal="0,0,1" radius="0.3" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.8"/>
                <planecontainer origin="0.6,1.92,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>P1</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="1.3,1.15,0; 1.6600000000000001,1.15,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="3"/>
                <circle center="2.45,1.15,0" normal="0,0,1" radius="0.3" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.8"/>
                <planecontainer origin="2.0500000000000003,1.92,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>P2</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="2.1500000000000004,1.15,0; 1.79,1.15,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="3"/>
                <lines pts="2.75,1.15,0; 3.1100000000000003,1.15,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="3"/>
                <circle center="3.9,1.15,0" normal="0,0,1" radius="0.3" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.8"/>
                <planecontainer origin="3.5,1.92,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>P3</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="3.6,1.15,0; 3.2399999999999998,1.15,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="3"/>
                <lines pts="4.2,1.15,0; 4.56,1.15,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="3"/>
                <circle center="5.35,1.15,0" normal="0,0,1" radius="0.3" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.8"/>
                <planecontainer origin="4.949999999999999,1.92,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>P4</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="5.05,1.15,0; 4.6899999999999995,1.15,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="3"/>
                <planecontainer origin="1.4,0.33,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>F1</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="1.89,0.33,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>F2</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="2.85,0.33,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>F3</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="3.34,0.33,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>F4</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="4.3,0.33,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>F5</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="4.79,0.33,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>F6</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="0.52,2.45,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>End fins face inward; interior fins are opposed.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lineardim startpoint="1.0,1.45,0" endpoint="2.45,1.45,0" pointondimline="1.725,2.15,0" formula="PierWallFins.S_p to ft" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" fontsize="9" linethickness=".6"><num>5.000 ft</num></lineardim>
            </canvas>
  </embed><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="L_w = 17.75 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>L_w = 17.75 ft</expbody><expresult> = 17.750 ft</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Wall length — authoritative quantity input.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="t_w = 36 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>t_w = 36 in</expbody><expresult> = 36.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Wall thickness — not the four-foot cap width.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="H_w = 14.364583333333 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>H_w = 14.364583333333 ft</expbody><expresult> = 14.365 ft</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Wall height — source quantity, not the gross cap-plus-wall wind rectangle.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="γ_c = 150 pcf" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>γ_c = 150 pcf</expbody><expresult> = 150.000 pcf</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Reinforced-concrete unit weight.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="N_p = 4" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>N_p = 4</expbody><expresult> = 4.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Current pile count; this symmetric solution is restricted to four piles.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="S_p = 5 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>S_p = 5 ft</expbody><expresult> = 5.000 ft</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Current pile spacing; not changed to make the connection pass.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="D_p = 20 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>D_p = 20 in</expbody><expresult> = 20.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Current pipe outside diameter.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="t_pipe = 0.475 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>t_pipe = 0.475 in</expbody><expresult> = 0.475 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Pipe design thickness supplied for the separate local shell check.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="f_c = 5.5 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>f_c = 5.5 ksi</expbody><expresult> = 5.500 ksi</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Class IV concrete strength, live from Materials.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="f_y = 60 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>f_y = 60 ksi</expbody><expresult> = 60.000 ksi</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Reinforcing yield strength, live from Materials.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="E_s = 29000 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>E_s = 29000 ksi</expbody><expresult> = 29000.000 ksi</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Reinforcing elastic modulus, live from Materials.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="c_w = 3 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>c_w = 3 in</expbody><expresult> = 3.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Adopted wall-face cover, matching the current formed substructure cover. (FDOT SDG 1.4.2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="γ_s = 490 pcf" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>γ_s = 490 pcf</expbody><expresult> = 490.000 pcf</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Steel weight for the added fin and saddle.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="F_y = 50 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>F_y = 50 ksi</expbody><expresult> = 50.000 ksi</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Selected ASTM A709 Grade 50 fin steel.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="F_u = 65 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>F_u = 65 ksi</expbody><expresult> = 65.000 ksi</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Selected plate tensile strength.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="E_p = 29000 ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>E_p = 29000 ksi</expbody><expresult> = 29000.000 ksi</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Plate elastic modulus.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="π = pi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>π = pi</expbody><expresult> = 3.142</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Mathematical circle constant.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="6" keepwithnext="True">Selected connection geometry</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="Terrain_elev = 25.5264 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>Terrain_elev = 25.5264 ft</expbody><expresult> = 25.526 ft</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Terrain_elev (Bridge Geometry - 2 Beam)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="a_p = 8 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>a_p = 8 in</expbody><expresult> = 8.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Fin radial projection from nominal pipe tangent/root plane.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="h_p = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>h_p = 12 in</expbody><expresult> = 12.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Fin height at the root.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="t_p = 1 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>t_p = 1 in</expbody><expresult> = 1.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Selected fin thickness.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="n_h = 2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>n_h = 2</expbody><expresult> = 2.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Designated hairpins per fin.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="d_h = 0.625 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>d_h = 0.625 in</expbody><expresult> = 0.625 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Selected #5 hairpin diameter.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="A_h = 0.31 in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>A_h = 0.31 in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.310 in^2</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Nominal area of one #5 hairpin leg.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="x_h1 = 1.75 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>x_h1 = 1.75 in</expbody><expresult> = 1.750 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>First hairpin plane measured radially from fin root.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="x_h2 = 5.25 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>x_h2 = 5.25 in</expbody><expresult> = 5.250 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Second hairpin plane measured radially from fin root.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="L_s = 6 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>L_s = 6 in</expbody><expresult> = 6.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Selected saddle length, centered on the hairpin-group centroid.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="c_top = 24 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>c_top = 24 in</expbody><expresult> = 24.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Distance from outer hairpin crown to top of wall.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="z_tip = 6 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>z_tip = 6 in</expbody><expresult> = 6.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Hairpin lower-end elevation above wall bottom.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="e_y = 0.25 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>e_y = 0.25 in</expbody><expresult> = 0.250 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Adopted transverse resultant offset; both signs are checked.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="α_h = 0.6" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>α_h = 0.6</expbody><expresult> = 0.600</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Maximum local share assigned to either hairpin for actual wall loading.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="Ω_h = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>Ω_h = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Nominal-yield development multiplier, not a code load factor.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="T_pos = 2 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>T_pos = 2 in</expbody><expresult> = 2.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Required wall-region pile-position control for this trial detailing.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="g_place = 1.5 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>g_place = 1.5 in</expbody><expresult> = 1.500 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Adopted concrete-placement gap between innermost grid and pipe.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="z_wall_top = 40.769319044745 ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>z_wall_top = 40.769319044745 ft</expbody><expresult> = 40.769 ft</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Assumed wall top at the cap soffit.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="n_fin = 2*N_p-2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>n_fin = 2*N_p-2</expbody><expresult> = 6.000</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">One inward fin at each end pile; two opposed fins at each interior pile.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="e_h = (x_h1+x_h2)/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>e_h = (x_h1+x_h2)/2 to in</expbody><expresult> = 3.500 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Nominal resultant location when both hairpins reach specified yield.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_h = x_h2-x_h1 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_h = x_h2-x_h1 to in</expbody><expresult> = 3.500 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Radial spacing of the two hairpins on one fin.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="D_s = 6*d_h to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>D_s = 6*d_h to in</expbody><expresult> = 3.750 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Required round bearing-saddle diameter; no sharp plate-edge loading. (LRFD Table 5.10.2.3-1) (LRFD Table 5.10.2.3-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="z_seat = H_w-c_top-D_s-d_h to ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>z_seat = H_w-c_top-D_s-d_h to ft</expbody><expresult> = 12.000 ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Top of fin / bottom of nominal round saddle above wall bottom.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="z_root = z_seat-h_p/2 to ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>z_root = z_seat-h_p/2 to ft</expbody><expresult> = 11.500 ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Weld handoff reference at the middle of the full-height fin root.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="e_end = (L_w-(N_p-1)*S_p)/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>e_end = (L_w-(N_p-1)*S_p)/2 to in</expbody><expresult> = 16.500 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall end to outer pile centerline.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="c_pipe_end = e_end-D_p/2-T_pos to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>c_pipe_end = e_end-D_p/2-T_pos to in</expbody><expresult> = 4.500 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Minimum concrete end envelope at the adverse pile position.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="z_wall_bottom = z_wall_top-H_w to ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>z_wall_bottom = z_wall_top-H_w to ft</expbody><expresult> = 26.405 ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall-bottom elevation resulting from the retained source wall height.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Δ_ground = z_wall_bottom-Terrain_elev to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Δ_ground = z_wall_bottom-Terrain_elev to in</expbody><expresult> = 10.540 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Source wall-bottom offset from terrain; verify intended bottom elevation.</paragraph><table name="C006Box50" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A5" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box50R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">GEOMETRY QUALIFICATIONS</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box50R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">All six fins are in one upper row. There is no equal-sharing assumption between multiple vertical rows. Additional rows require a new distribution model.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box50R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Outside fins are omitted at the end piles because the source wall has a short end extension. The two hairpins lie in planes normal to the fin blade and wrap over a round bearing saddle; no rebar is welded.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box50R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The computed wall-bottom offset from terrain is retained and shown above. It is not silently repaired by changing the source wall height. Confirm whether the intended wall extends to or below grade.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box50R4" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The selected round saddle is additional steel, not the fin plate itself. Its positive bearing fit, lateral restraint, local contact behavior and any attachment weld are required details to be completed separately.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <section name="C006Work02" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006work02">Step 2. Gravity reactions and plate spacing</paragraph></section><table name="C006Box66" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A4" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box66R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">REACTION MODEL — DERIVED EQUILIBRIUM</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box66R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The force points are F1 to F6 from left to right. The five spans alternate La, Lb, La, Lb, La. Both overhangs have length ao. Source geometry must remain symmetric with four piles.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box66R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Actual gravity resultants use the selected adverse split consistently in the support stations and root moments. Uniform gravity and constant effective in-plane stiffness are used only to obtain a rational reaction set. Support settlements, nonuniform cracked stiffness and coupled pile-wall restraint are not represented. The model does not certify the deep-wall load-collection mechanism.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box66R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The three-moment equations below are derived mechanics, not code resistance equations. A separate matrix-beam solution is used to audit the supplied numerical results.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="γ_DC = 1.25" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>γ_DC = 1.25</expbody><expresult> = 1.250</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Maximum permanent structural dead-load factor used for strength. (LRFD Table 3.4.1-2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="e_actual = (1-α_h)*x_h1+α_h*x_h2 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>e_actual = (1-α_h)*x_h1+α_h*x_h2 to in</expbody><expresult> = 3.850 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Radial resultant for the selected adverse actual 60/40 hairpin split.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="r_f = D_p/2+e_actual to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>r_f = D_p/2+e_actual to in</expbody><expresult> = 13.850 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Actual gravity-resultant station measured from the pile centerline.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="r_nom = D_p/2+e_h to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>r_nom = D_p/2+e_h to in</expbody><expresult> = 13.500 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Nominal equal-yield group center measured from the pile centerline.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_fin_nom = S_p-2*r_nom to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_fin_nom = S_p-2*r_nom to in</expbody><expresult> = 33.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Nominal equal-yield group spacing between adjacent piles.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_pipe_nom = 2*r_nom to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_pipe_nom = 2*r_nom to in</expbody><expresult> = 27.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Nominal equal-yield group spacing across an interior pile.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="L_a = S_p-2*r_f to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>L_a = S_p-2*r_f to in</expbody><expresult> = 32.300 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Clear span between fin-group force points in adjacent pile bays.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="L_b = 2*r_f to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>L_b = 2*r_f to in</expbody><expresult> = 27.700 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Force-point spacing across an interior pipe.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="a_o = e_end+r_f to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>a_o = e_end+r_f to in</expbody><expresult> = 30.350 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall-end overhang to the first/last hairpin-group force point.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="W_w = L_w*t_w*H_w*γ_c to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>W_w = L_w*t_w*H_w*γ_c to kip</expbody><expresult> = 114.737 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Conservative gross wall weight; pile displacement is not deducted.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="w_g = W_w/L_w to kip/ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>w_g = W_w/L_w to kip/ft</expbody><expresult> = 6.464 kip/ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Unfactored uniform wall gravity line load.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="W_p = a_p*h_p*t_p*γ_s to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>W_p = a_p*h_p*t_p*γ_s to kip</expbody><expresult> = 0.027 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">One fin-plate self-weight.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="W_s = π*D_s^2*L_s*γ_s/4 to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>W_s = π*D_s^2*L_s*γ_s/4 to kip</expbody><expresult> = 0.019 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">One solid round saddle self-weight (gross before machining).</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="W_a = W_p+W_s to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>W_a = W_p+W_s to kip</expbody><expresult> = 0.046 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Added steel per fin assembly.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_0 = -w_g*a_o^2/2 to kip*in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_0 = -w_g*a_o^2/2 to kip*in</expbody><expresult> = -248.091 kip*in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">End support moment produced by each wall overhang.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="K_11 = 2*(L_a+L_b) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>K_11 = 2*(L_a+L_b) to in</expbody><expresult> = 120.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">First symmetric three-moment coefficient.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="K_12 = L_b to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>K_12 = L_b to in</expbody><expresult> = 27.700 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Off-diagonal three-moment coefficient.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="K_22 = 2*L_b+3*L_a to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>K_22 = 2*L_b+3*L_a to in</expbody><expresult> = 152.300 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Second symmetric three-moment coefficient.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="B_1 = -w_g*(L_a^3+L_b^3)/4-M_0*L_a to kip*in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>B_1 = -w_g*(L_a^3+L_b^3)/4-M_0*L_a to kip*in^2</expbody><expresult> = 613.051 kip*in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">First moment-equation right-hand side.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="B_2 = -w_g*(L_a^3+L_b^3)/4 to kip*in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>B_2 = -w_g*(L_a^3+L_b^3)/4 to kip*in^2</expbody><expresult> = -7400.301 kip*in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Second moment-equation right-hand side.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Δ_K = K_11*K_22-K_12^2 to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Δ_K = K_11*K_22-K_12^2 to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 17508.710 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Determinant of the reduced symmetric system.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_1 = (B_1*K_22-B_2*K_12)/Δ_K to kip*in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_1 = (B_1*K_22-B_2*K_12)/Δ_K to kip*in</expbody><expresult> = 17.040 kip*in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Moment at F2 and F5.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_2 = (K_11*B_2-K_12*B_1)/Δ_K to kip*in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_2 = (K_11*B_2-K_12*B_1)/Δ_K to kip*in</expbody><expresult> = -51.690 kip*in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Moment at F3 and F4.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="R_1 = w_g*a_o+w_g*L_a/2+(M_1-M_0)/L_a to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>R_1 = w_g*a_o+w_g*L_a/2+(M_1-M_0)/L_a to kip</expbody><expresult> = 33.257 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Unfactored wall reaction at F1 and F6.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="R_2 = w_g*(L_a+L_b)/2+(M_0-M_1)/L_a+(M_2-M_1)/L_b to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>R_2 = w_g*(L_a+L_b)/2+(M_0-M_1)/L_a+(M_2-M_1)/L_b to kip</expbody><expresult> = 5.471 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Unfactored wall reaction at F2 and F5.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="R_3 = w_g*(L_b+L_a)/2+(M_1-M_2)/L_b to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>R_3 = w_g*(L_b+L_a)/2+(M_1-M_2)/L_b to kip</expbody><expresult> = 18.641 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Unfactored wall reaction at F3 and F4.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="R_max = Max(R_1,R_2,R_3) to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>R_max = Max(R_1,R_2,R_3) to kip</expbody><expresult> = 33.257 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Largest actual wall reaction before load factors.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_h_u = γ_DC*R_max to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_h_u = γ_DC*R_max to kip</expbody><expresult> = 41.571 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Governing factored wall load entering one designated hairpin group.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_reactions = If(Abs(2*(R_1+R_2+R_3)-W_w)&lt;0.000001 kip, &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_reactions = If(Abs(2*(R_1+R_2+R_3)-W_w)&lt;0.000001 kip, "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Six wall reactions reproduce the gross wall weight.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_model = If(And(N_p==4,n_h==2,α_h&gt;=0.5,α_h&lt;=1,L_a&gt;0 in,L_b&gt;0 in,a_o&gt;=0 in,Min(R_1,R_2,R_3)&gt;=0 kip), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_model = If(And(N_p==4,n_h==2,α_h&gt;=0.5,α_h&lt;=1,L_a&gt;0 in,L_b&gt;0 in,a_o&gt;=0 in,Min(R_1,R_2,R_3)&gt;=0 kip), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Validity of the symmetric four-pile/six-fin reaction model.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_saddle = If(And(x_h1&gt;0 in,x_h2&lt;a_p,L_s/2&gt;=s_h/2+d_h,e_h-L_s/2&gt;=0 in,e_h+L_s/2&lt;=a_p), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_saddle = If(And(x_h1&gt;0 in,x_h2&lt;a_p,L_s/2&gt;=s_h/2+d_h,e_h-L_s/2&gt;=0 in,e_h+L_s/2&lt;=a_p), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Selected saddle and hairpin force points fit on the fin projection.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="x_F1 = a_o to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>x_F1 = a_o to in</expbody><expresult> = 30.350 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall station of F1 force point.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="x_F2 = a_o+L_a to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>x_F2 = a_o+L_a to in</expbody><expresult> = 62.650 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall station of F2 force point.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="x_F3 = a_o+L_a+L_b to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>x_F3 = a_o+L_a+L_b to in</expbody><expresult> = 90.350 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall station of F3 force point.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="x_F4 = a_o+2*L_a+L_b to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>x_F4 = a_o+2*L_a+L_b to in</expbody><expresult> = 122.650 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall station of F4 force point.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="x_F5 = a_o+2*L_a+2*L_b to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>x_F5 = a_o+2*L_a+2*L_b to in</expbody><expresult> = 150.350 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall station of F5 force point.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="x_F6 = L_w-a_o to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>x_F6 = L_w-a_o to in</expbody><expresult> = 182.650 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall station of F6 force point.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="6" keepwithnext="True">Six-fin reaction schedule</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C" fontweight="bold" keepwithnext="True">Six-fin reaction schedule</paragraph><embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="8"><table name="C006Table90" capture="False" colwidths="1:108, 2:108, 3:108, 4:108, 5:108"><stylerule range="A1:E7" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" valueformat="RoundedNumber(3, 3, {PriorityUnits: []})" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#6A9075&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.4, &quot;#6A9075&quot;);"/><stylerule range="A1:E1" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center"/><stylerule range="B2:E7" horzalign="Center" vertalign="Center"/><row><textcell name="C006Table90R0C0" capture="False" background="#DCECE0"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">Fin</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R0C1" capture="False" background="#DCECE0"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">Pile / direction</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R0C2" capture="False" background="#DCECE0"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">Wall station</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R0C3" capture="False" background="#DCECE0"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">DC wall</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R0C4" capture="False" background="#DCECE0"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" fontweight="bold" horzalign="Center">Strength I / III wall</paragraph></textcell></row><row><textcell name="C006Table90R1C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">F1</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R1C1" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" horzalign="Center">P1 inward +X</paragraph></textcell><c formula="x_F1 to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>30.350 in</num></c><c formula="R_1 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>33.257 kip</num></c><c formula="γ_DC*R_1 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>41.571 kip</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table90R2C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">F2</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R2C1" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" horzalign="Center">P2 toward -X</paragraph></textcell><c formula="x_F2 to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>62.650 in</num></c><c formula="R_2 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>5.471 kip</num></c><c formula="γ_DC*R_2 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>6.838 kip</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table90R3C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">F3</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R3C1" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" horzalign="Center">P2 toward +X</paragraph></textcell><c formula="x_F3 to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>90.350 in</num></c><c formula="R_3 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>18.641 kip</num></c><c formula="γ_DC*R_3 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>23.302 kip</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table90R4C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">F4</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R4C1" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" horzalign="Center">P3 toward -X</paragraph></textcell><c formula="x_F4 to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>122.650 in</num></c><c formula="R_3 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>18.641 kip</num></c><c formula="γ_DC*R_3 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>23.302 kip</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table90R5C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">F5</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R5C1" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" horzalign="Center">P3 toward +X</paragraph></textcell><c formula="x_F5 to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>150.350 in</num></c><c formula="R_2 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>5.471 kip</num></c><c formula="γ_DC*R_2 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>6.838 kip</num></c></row><row><textcell name="C006Table90R6C0" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0">F6</paragraph></textcell><textcell name="C006Table90R6C1" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="0" horzalign="Center">P4 inward -X</paragraph></textcell><c formula="x_F6 to in" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>182.650 in</num></c><c formula="R_1 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>33.257 kip</num></c><c formula="γ_DC*R_1 to kip" capture="False" background="#EFF7F1"><num>41.571 kip</num></c></row></table></embed><section name="C006Work03" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006work03">Step 3. Hairpins and development</paragraph></section><embed spacingbefore="4" spacingafter="5"><canvas name="C006Hairpin" title="Hairpin section normal to fin" unit="in" size="6.5 in; 3.2 in; scaletofit">
                <include target="Library.Geometry"/>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15,2.98,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>HAIRPIN SECTION NORMAL TO FIN</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15,0.07,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#65717A"><textvalue>NOT TO SCALE — force signs follow the defined local axes.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="2.7,0.7,0; 3.45,0.7,0; 3.45,1.55,0; 2.7,1.55,0; 2.7,0.7,0" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="1.5"/>
                <circle center="3.075,1.95,0" normal="0,0,1" radius="0.4" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="1.5"/>
                <lines pts="3.545,0.45,0; 3.545,1.95,0; 3.545,1.95,0; 3.543475934823079,1.9878192872968612,0; 3.5389136234398193,2.025393302003147,0; 3.5313426541902446,2.062478362215152,0; 3.5208121277151587,2.098833957086692,0; 3.5073903385196474,2.134224306634235,0; 3.491164332057009,2.168419890860571,0; 3.472239340205584,2.2011989382800663,0; 3.4507380987996457,2.23234886419185,0; 3.426800051640418,2.2616676493731735,0; 3.4005804461495117,2.2889651502515926,0; 3.3722493265298277,2.3140643320589978,0; 3.3419904309636435,2.3368024169700186,0; 3.31,2.357031939778686,0; 3.2764855038594356,2.37462170426688,0; 3.241664296909992,2.3894576340621447,0; 3.205762208040733,2.401443512466745,0; 3.169012076074741,2.410501606459866,0; 3.131652239720002,2.4165731708260854,0; 3.0939249918514253,2.4196188291406378,0; 3.056075008148575,2.4196188291406378,0; 3.0183477602799984,2.4165731708260854,0; 2.9809879239252592,2.410501606459866,0; 2.9442377919592677,2.401443512466745,0; 2.9083357030900086,2.3894576340621447,0; 2.8735144961405648,2.37462170426688,0; 2.8400000000000003,2.357031939778686,0; 2.808009569036357,2.3368024169700186,0; 2.777750673470173,2.3140643320589978,0; 2.7494195538504886,2.2889651502515926,0; 2.723199948359583,2.261667649373174,0; 2.6992619012003547,2.23234886419185,0; 2.6777606597944166,2.2011989382800667,0; 2.6588356679429914,2.168419890860571,0; 2.642609661480353,2.1342243066342355,0; 2.6291878722848416,2.098833957086692,0; 2.6186573458097557,2.062478362215152,0; 2.611086376560181,2.0253933020031476,0; 2.6065240651769215,1.9878192872968612,0; 2.6050000000000004,1.95,0; 2.605,0.45,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1.8"/>
                <planecontainer origin="0.2,2.72,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>View through one hairpin plane.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="0.2,2.34,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Round saddle required:</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lineardim startpoint="2.675,1.95,0" endpoint="3.475,1.95,0" pointondimline="3.075,2.65,0" formula="PierWallFins.D_s to in" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" fontsize="9" linethickness=".6"><num>3.750 in</num></lineardim>
                <planecontainer origin="0.2,1.65,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Fin plate beneath the saddle</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="2.0,1.65,0; 2.7,1.25,0" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.6"/>
                <planecontainer origin="4.05,2.0,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Curved contact</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="4.0,1.94,0; 3.45,2.1,0" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.6"/>
                <planecontainer origin="4.05,1.35,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Both legs extend</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="4.05,1.15,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>into the wall.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <arrowlines pts="2.605,1.05,0; 2.605,0.55,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <arrowlines pts="3.545,1.05,0; 3.545,0.55,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
            </canvas>
  </embed><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_h = 0.75" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_h = 0.75</expbody><expresult> = 0.750</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Adopted hanger resistance factor; conservative relative to the 0.90 LRFD STM tie factor. (LRFD 5.5.4.2; 5.8.2.4)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="λ_rl = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>λ_rl = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Hairpin legs are vertical; no horizontal top-bar factor.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="λ_cf = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>λ_cf = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Uncoated hairpins; re-evaluate when coating changes.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="λ_rc = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>λ_rc = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>No beneficial confinement reduction used for straight development.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="λ_er = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>λ_er = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Full specified yield is developed; no excess-area reduction.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="λ_c = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>λ_c = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Normal-weight concrete modifier. (LRFD 5.4.2.8)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="F_head = 0 kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>F_head = 0 kip</expbody><expresult> = 0.000 kip</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>No head or hooked-end force credited at the straight hairpin tails.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="l_zone = 36 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>l_zone = 36 in</expbody><expresult> = 36.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Reserved disturbed/transfer region below the fin seat; tail development starts below this region.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_group = 2*n_h*A_h to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_group = 2*n_h*A_h to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 1.240 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Effective tensile area of the designated hairpin group.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="P_n_one = 2*A_h*f_y to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>P_n_one = 2*A_h*f_y to kip</expbody><expresult> = 37.200 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Nominal yield resistance of one two-legged hairpin.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="P_r_one = φ_h*P_n_one to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>P_r_one = φ_h*P_n_one to kip</expbody><expresult> = 27.900 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Factored resistance of one fully developed hairpin.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="P_n_group = A_group*f_y to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>P_n_group = A_group*f_y to kip</expbody><expresult> = 74.400 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Full nominal yield resistance of both designated hairpins.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="P_r_group = φ_h*P_n_group to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>P_r_group = φ_h*P_n_group to kip</expbody><expresult> = 55.800 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Factored design resistance of the two-hairpin group.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="P_one_u = α_h*V_h_u to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>P_one_u = α_h*V_h_u to kip</expbody><expresult> = 24.942 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Demand on the more heavily loaded hairpin for actual wall loading.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="DC_hairpin = P_one_u/P_r_one" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>DC_hairpin = P_one_u/P_r_one</expbody><expresult> = 0.894</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Individual-hairpin utilization including the 60/40 local split.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="P_target = Ω_h*P_n_group to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>P_target = Ω_h*P_n_group to kip</expbody><expresult> = 74.400 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Separate full-yield development target for the fin and external connection checks.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="l_db = 0.17*d_h*((λ_er*f_y-F_head/A_h)/(1 ksi)/(1.97*λ_c*Sqrt(Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi)))))^2 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>l_db = 0.17*d_h*((λ_er*f_y-F_head/A_h)/(1 ksi)/(1.97*λ_c*Sqrt(Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi)))))^2 to in</expbody><expresult> = 42.026 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Basic straight-tail development length, using the 10th-edition expression. (LRFD Eq. 5.10.8.2.1a-2) (LRFD Eq. 5.10.8.2.1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="l_d = Max(12 in,l_db*λ_rl*λ_cf*λ_rc) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>l_d = Max(12 in,l_db*λ_rl*λ_cf*λ_rc) to in</expbody><expresult> = 42.026 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Required straight-tail development length for full yield. (LRFD Eq. 5.10.8.2.1a-1) (LRFD Eq. 5.10.8.2.1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="l_av = z_seat-l_zone-z_tip to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>l_av = z_seat-l_zone-z_tip to in</expbody><expresult> = 102.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Available straight tail beyond the reserved transfer region.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="L_leg = z_seat+D_s/2-z_tip to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>L_leg = z_seat+D_s/2-z_tip to in</expbody><expresult> = 139.875 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Approximate tangent-leg length to the crown springline.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="L_bar = 2*L_leg+π*(D_s+d_h)/2 to ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>L_bar = 2*L_leg+π*(D_s+d_h)/2 to ft</expbody><expresult> = 23.885 ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Nominal centerline hairpin length before fabrication allowances.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_hairpin = If(And(DC_hairpin&lt;=1,V_h_u&lt;=P_r_group), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_hairpin = If(And(DC_hairpin&lt;=1,V_h_u&lt;=P_r_group), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Hairpin tensile resistance under assigned actual gravity loads.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_development = If(l_av&gt;=l_d, &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_development = If(l_av&gt;=l_d, "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Available straight-tail length exceeds the full-yield requirement.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_bend = If(D_s&gt;=6*d_h, &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_bend = If(D_s&gt;=6*d_h, "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Hairpin inside bend diameter satisfies the general #5 bar minimum. (LRFD Table 5.10.2.3-1) (LRFD Table 5.10.2.3-1)</paragraph><table name="C006Box116" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A4" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box116R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">REQUIRED LOCAL DETAIL — NOT A SHARP-EDGE HANGER</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box116R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Two inverted-U #5 hairpins wrap a round steel bearing saddle above each fin. Hairpins are normal to the fin plane; the fin lies between their legs. Use a fitted bearing seat and positive saddle retention. Do not weld the reinforcing bars.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box116R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The tail-length and steel-area checks above are completed. The local saddle bearing/contact, concrete load collection into those tails and local strut/node confinement must still establish the assumed load path; they are not certified by the area-times-yield calculation.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box116R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">General face-grid bars are not included in the designated hairpin yield target. Additional connected bars that can impose force on the fin require updating the interface demand.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <section name="C006Work04" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006work04">Step 4. Fin plate resistance</paragraph></section><embed spacingbefore="4" spacingafter="5"><canvas name="C006Root" title="Fin-root free body for external weld calculation" unit="in" size="6.5 in; 3.1 in; scaletofit">
                <include target="Library.Geometry"/>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15,2.88,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>FIN-ROOT FREE BODY FOR EXTERNAL WELD CALCULATION</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15,0.07,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#65717A"><textvalue>NOT TO SCALE — force signs follow the defined local axes.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="1.0,0.55,0; 1.0,2.45,0" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="3"/>
                <lines pts="1.0,0.7,0; 4.3,0.7,0; 4.3,2.15,0; 1.0,2.15,0" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="1"/>
                <circle center="1.0,1.425,0" normal="0,0,1" radius="0.035" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="0.8"/>
                <arrowlines pts="2.45,2.65,0; 2.45,2.15,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1.3" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <planecontainer origin="2.58,2.49,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Vertical hairpin-group force</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <arrowlines pts="1.0,1.425,0; 1.75,1.425,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.7" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <planecontainer origin="1.45,1.57,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#1766A0"><textvalue>+x outward</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <arrowlines pts="1.0,1.425,0; 1.0,0.95,0" linecolor="#1766A0" linethickness="0.7" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <planecontainer origin="0.2,0.85,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#1766A0"><textvalue>+z down</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lineardim startpoint="1,0.7,0" endpoint="4.3,0.7,0" pointondimline="2.65,0.32,0" formula="PierWallFins.a_p to in" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" fontsize="9" linethickness=".6"><num>8.000 in</num></lineardim>
                <lineardim startpoint="4.3,0.7,0" endpoint="4.3,2.15,0" pointondimline="4.65,1.425,0" formula="PierWallFins.h_p to in" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" fontsize="9" linethickness=".6"><num>12.000 in</num></lineardim>
                <planecontainer origin="4.95,2.35,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Root origin O</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="4.95,2.13,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>at midheight.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="4.95,1.6,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Fz positive</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="4.95,1.38,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>My negative</textvalue></planecontainer>
            </canvas>
  </embed><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_f = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_f = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Steel flexure resistance factor. (LRFD 6.5.4.2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_v = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_v = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Steel shear-yielding resistance factor. (LRFD 6.5.4.2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_vu = 0.8" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_vu = 0.8</expbody><expresult> = 0.800</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Steel connection-element shear-rupture resistance factor. (LRFD 6.5.4.2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="C_b = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>C_b = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>No favorable moment-gradient enhancement.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_target = P_target+γ_DC*W_a to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_target = P_target+γ_DC*W_a to kip</expbody><expresult> = 74.458 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Fin-root vertical force for the hairpin-yield target plus factored local steel weight.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_y_target = P_target*e_h+γ_DC*(W_p*a_p/2+W_s*e_h) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_y_target = P_target*e_h+γ_DC*(W_p*a_p/2+W_s*e_h) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 21.718 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Magnitude of major-axis root moment for the yield target.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_x_target = P_target*e_y to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_x_target = P_target*e_y to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 1.550 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Magnitude of minor-axis root moment for the transverse offset.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_actual = V_h_u+γ_DC*W_a to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_actual = V_h_u+γ_DC*W_a to kip</expbody><expresult> = 41.628 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Governing actual factored fin-root shear.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_y_actual = V_h_u*e_actual+γ_DC*(W_p*a_p/2+W_s*e_h) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_y_actual = V_h_u*e_actual+γ_DC*(W_p*a_p/2+W_s*e_h) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 13.355 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Major-axis moment for the governing actual wall reaction.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_x_actual = V_h_u*e_y to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_x_actual = V_h_u*e_y to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 0.866 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Minor-axis moment for the governing actual wall reaction.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_d = Max(V_target,V_actual) to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_d = Max(V_target,V_actual) to kip</expbody><expresult> = 74.458 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Plate shear sizing demand; governing demand family identified below.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_yd = Max(M_y_target,M_y_actual) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_yd = Max(M_y_target,M_y_actual) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 21.718 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Plate major-axis sizing moment.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_xd = Max(M_x_target,M_x_actual) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_xd = Max(M_x_target,M_x_actual) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 1.550 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Plate minor-axis sizing moment.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="S_y = t_p*h_p^2/6 to in^3" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>S_y = t_p*h_p^2/6 to in^3</expbody><expresult> = 24.000 in^3</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Rectangular root section modulus for vertical in-plane loading.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="S_x = h_p*t_p^2/6 to in^3" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>S_x = h_p*t_p^2/6 to in^3</expbody><expresult> = 2.000 in^3</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Rectangular root section modulus for transverse eccentricity.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Z_y = t_p*h_p^2/4 to in^3" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Z_y = t_p*h_p^2/4 to in^3</expbody><expresult> = 36.000 in^3</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Major-axis plastic section modulus.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_Y = F_y*S_y to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_Y = F_y*S_y to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 100.000 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Major-axis elastic yield moment.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_P = Min(F_y*Z_y,1.6*M_Y) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_P = Min(F_y*Z_y,1.6*M_Y) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 150.000 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Yield-based nominal flexural resistance. (LRFD Eq. 6.12.2.2.7-1) (LRFD Eq. 6.12.2.2.7-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="L_buck = 2*a_p to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>L_buck = 2*a_p to in</expbody><expresult> = 16.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Conservative unbraced length for the cantilever fin; no concrete-restraint credit.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="λ_LT = L_buck*h_p/t_p^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>λ_LT = L_buck*h_p/t_p^2</expbody><expresult> = 192.000</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Rectangular-bar LTB slenderness parameter.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="λ_p = 0.08*E_p/F_y" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>λ_p = 0.08*E_p/F_y</expbody><expresult> = 46.400</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Yield-region LTB threshold. (LRFD 6.12.2.2.7) (LRFD 6.12.2.2.7)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="λ_r = 1.9*E_p/F_y" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>λ_r = 1.9*E_p/F_y</expbody><expresult> = 1102.000</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Elastic-region LTB threshold. (LRFD 6.12.2.2.7) (LRFD 6.12.2.2.7)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_LTB = If(λ_LT&lt;=λ_p,M_P,If(λ_LT&lt;=λ_r,Min(M_P,C_b*(1.52-0.274*λ_LT*F_y/E_p)*M_Y),Min(M_P,1.9*E_p*C_b*S_y/λ_LT))) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_LTB = If(λ_LT&lt;=λ_p,M_P,If(λ_LT&lt;=λ_r,Min(M_P,C_b*(1.52-0.274*λ_LT*F_y/E_p)*M_Y),Min(M_P,1.9*E_p*C_b*S_y/λ_LT))) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 142.930 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">LTB-limited nominal major-axis resistance. (LRFD Eqs. 6.12.2.2.7-2 through -4) (LRFD Eq. 6.12.2.2.7-2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_ry = φ_f*Min(M_Y,M_LTB) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_ry = φ_f*Min(M_Y,M_LTB) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 100.000 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Adopted major-axis resistance; limited further to first yield.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_rx = φ_f*F_y*S_x to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_rx = φ_f*F_y*S_x to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 8.333 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Adopted minor-axis resistance, conservatively limited to first yield. (LRFD 6.12.2.2.7) (LRFD 6.12.2.2.7)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_v = t_p*h_p to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_v = t_p*h_p to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 12.000 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Full unperforated root shear area.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="R_vy = φ_v*0.58*F_y*A_v to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>R_vy = φ_v*0.58*F_y*A_v to kip</expbody><expresult> = 348.000 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Factored shear-yielding resistance. (LRFD Eq. 6.13.5.3-1) (LRFD Eq. 6.13.5.3-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="R_vu = φ_vu*0.58*F_u*A_v to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>R_vu = φ_vu*0.58*F_u*A_v to kip</expbody><expresult> = 361.920 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Factored shear-rupture resistance; no holes and Rp = 1. (LRFD Eq. 6.13.5.3-2) (LRFD Eq. 6.13.5.3-2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="R_v = Min(R_vy,R_vu) to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>R_v = Min(R_vy,R_vu) to kip</expbody><expresult> = 348.000 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Adopted fin-root shear resistance.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="DC_biax = M_yd/M_ry+M_xd/M_rx" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>DC_biax = M_yd/M_ry+M_xd/M_rx</expbody><expresult> = 0.403</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Conservative linear biaxial first-yield utilization.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="σ_b = M_yd/S_y+M_xd/S_x to ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>σ_b = M_yd/S_y+M_xd/S_x to ksi</expbody><expresult> = 20.159 ksi</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Conservative maximum combined elastic normal stress.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="τ_max = 1.5*V_d/A_v to ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>τ_max = 1.5*V_d/A_v to ksi</expbody><expresult> = 9.307 ksi</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Rectangular-section maximum elastic shear stress.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="σ_VM = Sqrt(σ_b^2+3*τ_max^2) to ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>σ_VM = Sqrt(σ_b^2+3*τ_max^2) to ksi</expbody><expresult> = 25.812 ksi</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Conservative von Mises screen, using separate maxima at a common point.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="DC_VM = σ_VM/F_y" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>DC_VM = σ_VM/F_y</expbody><expresult> = 0.516</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Additional elastic combined-stress utilization.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="DC_plate = Max(DC_biax,DC_VM,V_d/R_v)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>DC_plate = Max(DC_biax,DC_VM,V_d/R_v)</expbody><expresult> = 0.516</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Largest implemented plate utilization.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_plate_flex = If(DC_biax&lt;=1, &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_plate_flex = If(DC_biax&lt;=1, "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Selected fin satisfies adopted biaxial elastic/LTB resistance.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_plate_shear = If(V_d&lt;=R_v, &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_plate_shear = If(V_d&lt;=R_v, "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Selected fin satisfies root shear yielding and rupture.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_plate_VM = If(DC_VM&lt;=1, &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_plate_VM = If(DC_VM&lt;=1, "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Selected fin passes additional conservative combined-stress screen.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_root = If(And(t_p&gt;0 in,h_p&gt;0 in,a_p&gt;0 in,h_p&lt;=z_seat), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_root = If(And(t_p&gt;0 in,h_p&gt;0 in,a_p&gt;0 in,h_p&lt;=z_seat), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Plate geometry remains valid and inside the source wall.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#A64A20">No root copes, holes, slots, or unverified effective-width reductions are allowed within the checked root section. Plate-to-pipe local punching/tearing and the weld-adjacent base-metal paths are completion checks at the interface, not included in this isolated plate result.</paragraph> <section name="C006Work05" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006work05">Step 5. Out-of-plane wall strip</paragraph></section><embed spacingbefore="4" spacingafter="5"><canvas name="C006WindStrip" title="One-foot horizontal wind strip in plan" unit="in" size="6.5 in; 3.0 in; scaletofit">
                <include target="Library.Geometry"/>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15,2.78,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>ONE-FOOT HORIZONTAL WIND STRIP IN PLAN</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="0.15,0.07,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#65717A"><textvalue>NOT TO SCALE — force signs follow the defined local axes.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lines pts="1.0,0.85,0; 5.2,0.85,0; 5.2,1.65,0; 1.0,1.65,0; 1.0,0.85,0" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="1"/>
                <circle center="1.0,1.25,0" normal="0,0,1" radius="0.34" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.8"/>
                <circle center="5.2,1.25,0" normal="0,0,1" radius="0.34" linecolor="#29333D" linethickness="0.8"/>
                <arrowlines pts="1.65,2.15,0; 1.65,1.7,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <arrowlines pts="2.35,2.15,0; 2.35,1.7,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <arrowlines pts="3.05,2.15,0; 3.05,1.7,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <arrowlines pts="3.75,2.15,0; 3.75,1.7,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <arrowlines pts="4.45,2.15,0; 4.45,1.7,0" linecolor="#B5443C" linethickness="1" endarrow="5; 2.5"/>
                <planecontainer origin="1.7,2.35,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Uniform wind; also check the reversed direction.</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <lineardim startpoint="1.0,0.9,0" endpoint="5.2,0.9,0" pointondimline="3.1,0.47,0" formula="PierWallFins.L_strip to ft" linecolor="#1766A0" textcolor="#1766A0" fontsize="9" linethickness=".6"><num>5.000 ft</num></lineardim>
                <planecontainer origin="0.3,0.2,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Pile contact</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="4.85,0.2,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Pile contact</textvalue></planecontainer>
                <planecontainer origin="1.9,1.05,0" dir="1,0,0" normal="0,0,1" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="8" textcolor="#29333D"><textvalue>Wall strip height = one foot (out of this view)</textvalue></planecontainer>
            </canvas>
  </embed><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="p_III = 0.05999919582 ksf" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>p_III = 0.05999919582 ksf</expbody><expresult> = 0.060 ksf</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Strength III direct substructure pressure, before WS factor.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="p_I = 0.01705984 ksf" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>p_I = 0.01705984 ksf</expbody><expresult> = 0.017 ksf</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Service I direct substructure pressure.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="γ_WS = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>γ_WS = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>WS factor for these separate direct-wind pressure sets. (LRFD Table 3.4.1-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="b_strip = 12 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>b_strip = 12 in</expbody><expresult> = 12.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Vertical height of the out-of-plane wall strip.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="d_grid = 0.75 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>d_grid = 0.75 in</expbody><expresult> = 0.750 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Selected #6 distributed wall-grid diameter.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="A_grid = 0.44 in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>A_grid = 0.44 in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.440 in^2</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Nominal area of one #6 wall-grid bar.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="s_grid = 8 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>s_grid = 8 in</expbody><expresult> = 8.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Horizontal and vertical face-grid spacing, each face.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="φ_rc = 0.9" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>φ_rc = 0.9</expbody><expresult> = 0.900</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Tension-controlled reinforced-concrete resistance factor. (LRFD 5.5.4.2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="γ_1 = 1.6" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>γ_1 = 1.6</expbody><expresult> = 1.600</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Cracking variability factor for nonsegmental concrete. (LRFD 5.6.3.3)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="γ_3 = 0.67" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>γ_3 = 0.67</expbody><expresult> = 0.670</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Yield-to-ultimate factor for ASTM A615 Grade 60 reinforcing. (LRFD 5.6.3.3)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="d_tie = 0.5 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>d_tie = 0.5 in</expbody><expresult> = 0.500 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Selected #4 cross-tie diameter.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="A_tie = 0.2 in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>A_tie = 0.2 in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.200 in^2</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Area of one through-thickness cross-tie leg.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="s_tie = 8 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>s_tie = 8 in</expbody><expresult> = 8.000 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Cross-tie spacing along span and vertically.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="β_v = 2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>β_v = 2</expbody><expresult> = 2.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Simplified shear parameter with at least minimum transverse steel. (LRFD 5.7.3.4.1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="K_1 = 1" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>K_1 = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Default aggregate correction factor in the absence of approved measured data. (LRFD 5.4.2.4)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="w_c_E = 145 pcf" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>w_c_E = 145 pcf</expbody><expresult> = 145.000 pcf</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Plain-concrete unit weight for modulus; excludes the reinforcing weight allowance.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="L_strip = S_p to ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>L_strip = S_p to ft</expbody><expresult> = 5.000 ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Conservative support-center span for horizontal wall strips.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="q_III = γ_WS*p_III*b_strip to kip/ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>q_III = γ_WS*p_III*b_strip to kip/ft</expbody><expresult> = 0.060 kip/ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Strength III line load on one horizontal strip.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="q_I = p_I*b_strip to kip/ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>q_I = p_I*b_strip to kip/ft</expbody><expresult> = 0.017 kip/ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Service I line load on one horizontal strip.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_u_strip = q_III*Max(L_strip^2/8,e_end^2/2) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_u_strip = q_III*Max(L_strip^2/8,e_end^2/2) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 0.187 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Adopted reversible moment envelope including source wall overhang.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_u_strip = q_III*Max(L_strip,e_end) to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_u_strip = q_III*Max(L_strip,e_end) to kip</expbody><expresult> = 0.300 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Conservative strip shear/reaction bound.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_I_strip = q_I*Max(L_strip^2/8,e_end^2/2) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_I_strip = q_I*Max(L_strip^2/8,e_end^2/2) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 0.053 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Service moment using the same reversible envelope.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_strip = A_grid*b_strip/s_grid to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_strip = A_grid*b_strip/s_grid to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.660 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Horizontal tension steel in a one-foot strip at one face.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="d_strip = t_w-c_w-d_grid/2 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>d_strip = t_w-c_w-d_grid/2 to in</expbody><expresult> = 32.625 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Effective depth with horizontal bars outermost.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="β_1 = Max(0.65,Min(0.85,0.85-0.05*(f_c/(1 ksi)-4)))" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>β_1 = Max(0.65,Min(0.85,0.85-0.05*(f_c/(1 ksi)-4)))</expbody><expresult> = 0.775</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Rectangular concrete stress-block factor. (LRFD 5.6.2.2) (LRFD 5.6.2.2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="a_c = A_strip*f_y/(0.85*f_c*b_strip) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>a_c = A_strip*f_y/(0.85*f_c*b_strip) to in</expbody><expresult> = 0.706 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Equivalent stress-block depth.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="c_n = a_c/β_1 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>c_n = a_c/β_1 to in</expbody><expresult> = 0.911 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Neutral-axis depth at nominal flexural resistance.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="ε_t = 0.003*(d_strip-c_n)/c_n" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>ε_t = 0.003*(d_strip-c_n)/c_n</expbody><expresult> = 0.104</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Extreme tensile-bar strain at nominal resistance.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_r_strip = φ_rc*A_strip*f_y*(d_strip-a_c/2) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_r_strip = φ_rc*A_strip*f_y*(d_strip-a_c/2) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 95.848 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Factored flexural resistance of either face. (LRFD 5.6.3.2) (LRFD 5.6.3.2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="f_r = 0.24*λ_c*Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi))*(1 ksi) to ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>f_r = 0.24*λ_c*Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi))*(1 ksi) to ksi</expbody><expresult> = 0.563 ksi</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Modulus of rupture for the minimum-flexure and service applicability checks. (LRFD 5.4.2.6) (LRFD 5.4.2.6)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="S_g = b_strip*t_w^2/6 to in^3" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>S_g = b_strip*t_w^2/6 to in^3</expbody><expresult> = 2592.000 in^3</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Gross section modulus away from the pipe disturbed region.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_cr = γ_3*γ_1*f_r*S_g to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_cr = γ_3*γ_1*f_r*S_g to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 130.329 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Cracking moment for a nonprestressed, noncomposite section. (LRFD Eq. 5.6.3.3-1) (LRFD Eq. 5.6.3.3-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="M_min = Min(1.33*M_u_strip,M_cr) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>M_min = Min(1.33*M_u_strip,M_cr) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 0.249 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Required factored resistance for the minimum-flexural-reinforcement screen. (LRFD 5.6.3.3) (LRFD 5.6.3.3)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_v_strip = A_tie*b_strip/s_tie to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_v_strip = A_tie*b_strip/s_tie to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.300 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Through-thickness cross-tie area per longitudinal spacing in a unit strip.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_v_min = 0.0316*Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi))*b_strip*s_tie/(f_y/(1 ksi)) to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_v_min = 0.0316*Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi))*b_strip*s_tie/(f_y/(1 ksi)) to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.119 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Minimum transverse steel for use of the simplified shear parameters. (LRFD Eq. 5.7.2.5-1) (LRFD Eq. 5.7.2.5-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="d_v = Max(d_strip-a_c/2,0.9*d_strip,0.72*t_w) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>d_v = Max(d_strip-a_c/2,0.9*d_strip,0.72*t_w) to in</expbody><expresult> = 32.272 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Effective shear depth. (LRFD 5.7.2.8) (LRFD 5.7.2.8)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_c = 0.0316*β_v*λ_c*Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi))*(1 ksi)*b_strip*d_v to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_c = 0.0316*β_v*λ_c*Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi))*(1 ksi)*b_strip*d_v to kip</expbody><expresult> = 57.399 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Concrete shear contribution. (LRFD Eq. 5.7.3.3-3) (LRFD Eq. 5.7.3.3-3)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_s = A_v_strip*f_y*d_v/s_tie to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_s = A_v_strip*f_y*d_v/s_tie to kip</expbody><expresult> = 72.612 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Cross-tie contribution at theta = 45 degrees and alpha = 90 degrees. (LRFD Eq. 5.7.3.3-4) (LRFD Eq. 5.7.3.3-4)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_r_strip = 0.9*Min(V_c+V_s,0.25*f_c*b_strip*d_v) to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_r_strip = 0.9*Min(V_c+V_s,0.25*f_c*b_strip*d_v) to kip</expbody><expresult> = 117.010 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Factored wall-strip shear resistance. (LRFD Eqs. 5.7.3.3-1 and -2) (LRFD Eq. 5.7.3.3-1; LRFD 5.7.3.3-2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="f_t_gross = M_I_strip/S_g to ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>f_t_gross = M_I_strip/S_g to ksi</expbody><expresult> = 0.000 ksi</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Gross-section flexural tension at Service I.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="E_c = 120000*K_1*(w_c_E/(1000 pcf))^2*(f_c/(1 ksi))^0.33*(1 ksi) to ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>E_c = 120000*K_1*(w_c_E/(1000 pcf))^2*(f_c/(1 ksi))^0.33*(1 ksi) to ksi</expbody><expresult> = 4428.299 ksi</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Concrete modulus for the supplementary cracked-section service check. (LRFD Eq. 5.4.2.4-1) (LRFD Eq. 5.4.2.4-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="n_mod = E_s/E_c" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>n_mod = E_s/E_c</expbody><expresult> = 6.549</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Modular ratio for the supplementary cracked-section service check.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="c_cr = (Sqrt((n_mod*A_strip)^2+2*b_strip*n_mod*A_strip*d_strip)-n_mod*A_strip)/b_strip to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>c_cr = (Sqrt((n_mod*A_strip)^2+2*b_strip*n_mod*A_strip*d_strip)-n_mod*A_strip)/b_strip to in</expbody><expresult> = 4.501 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Cracked transformed-section neutral axis, compression steel neglected.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="f_ss = M_I_strip/(A_strip*(d_strip-c_cr/3)) to ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>f_ss = M_I_strip/(A_strip*(d_strip-c_cr/3)) to ksi</expbody><expresult> = 0.031 ksi</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Supplementary cracked-section tension-steel stress.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="β_s = 1+(c_w+d_grid/2)/(0.7*(t_w-c_w-d_grid/2))" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>β_s = 1+(c_w+d_grid/2)/(0.7*(t_w-c_w-d_grid/2))</expbody><expresult> = 1.148</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Service crack-spacing strain-gradient factor. (LRFD Eq. 5.6.7-2) (LRFD Eq. 5.6.7-2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_crack = 700/(β_s*(f_ss/(1 ksi)))*(1 in)-2*(c_w+d_grid/2) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_crack = 700/(β_s*(f_ss/(1 ksi)))*(1 in)-2*(c_w+d_grid/2) to in</expbody><expresult> = 19576.298 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Supplementary Class 1 flexural crack-control spacing limit. (LRFD Eq. 5.6.7-1; FDOT SDG 3.10.F) (LRFD Eq. 5.6.7-1; SDG 3.10.F)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="F_w_III = p_III*L_w*H_w to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>F_w_III = p_III*L_w*H_w to kip</expbody><expresult> = 15.298 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Strength III broad-face wind on the source wall alone.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_strip_flex = If(And(ε_t&gt;=0.005,M_u_strip&lt;=M_r_strip,M_min&lt;=M_r_strip), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_strip_flex = If(And(ε_t&gt;=0.005,M_u_strip&lt;=M_r_strip,M_min&lt;=M_r_strip), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wind-strip flexure and minimum flexural reinforcement.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="v_u_strip = V_u_strip/(φ_rc*b_strip*d_v) to ksi" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>v_u_strip = V_u_strip/(φ_rc*b_strip*d_v) to ksi</expbody><expresult> = 0.001 ksi</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Factored shear-stress parameter for transverse spacing. (LRFD 5.7.2.8) (LRFD 5.7.2.8)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_vmax = If(v_u_strip&lt;0.125*f_c,Min(0.8*d_v,24 in),Min(0.4*d_v,12 in)) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_vmax = If(v_u_strip&lt;0.125*f_c,Min(0.8*d_v,24 in),Min(0.4*d_v,12 in)) to in</expbody><expresult> = 24.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Maximum transverse reinforcement spacing. (LRFD Eqs. 5.7.2.6-1 and -2) (LRFD Eq. 5.7.2.6-1; LRFD 5.7.2.6-2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_strip_shear = If(And(A_v_strip&gt;=A_v_min,V_u_strip&lt;=V_r_strip,s_tie&lt;=s_vmax), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_strip_shear = If(And(A_v_strip&gt;=A_v_min,V_u_strip&lt;=V_r_strip,s_tie&lt;=s_vmax), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wind-strip shear and transverse reinforcement area/spacing.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_service = If(And(s_grid&lt;=s_crack,f_ss&lt;=0.8*f_y), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_service = If(And(s_grid&lt;=s_crack,f_ss&lt;=0.8*f_y), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Supplementary Service I cracked-section check with FDOT amendment.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Status_cracking = If(f_t_gross&lt;=0.8*f_r,&quot;Below LRFD 5.6.7 stress trigger&quot;,&quot;LRFD 5.6.7 check required&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Status_cracking = If(f_t_gross&lt;=0.8*f_r,"Below LRFD 5.6.7 stress trigger","LRFD 5.6.7 check required")</expbody><expresult> = Below LRFD 5.6.7 stress trigger</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Service crack-control applicability.</paragraph><table name="C006Box211" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A4" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box211R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">WALL-STRIP BOUNDARY</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box211R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The horizontal #6 bars are outermost at each broad face, followed by vertical #6 bars. Through-thickness #4 cross-ties must positively engage the face grids; ordinary in-plane vertical bars do not count as through-thickness shear reinforcement.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box211R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The checked solid strip applies between the pile disturbed regions. Do not apply its gross-section resistance through the pipe opening. Local pipe-contact concrete bearing/splitting and bar routing around the pile are separate release checks.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box211R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">The adopted wind moment is checked with bars at either face. Compatibility with pile movement and the global wall/cap interface is not demonstrated by these load-only strip calculations.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <section name="C006Work06" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006work06">Step 6. Distributed reinforcement and detailing</paragraph></section><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="ρ_STM = 0.003" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>ρ_STM = 0.003</expbody><expresult> = 0.003</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Adopted orthogonal grid minimum for potential wall disturbed regions. (LRFD 5.8.2.6)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="4" level="1"><dynexp formula="a_agg = 0.75 in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False" style="Required Input"><expbody>a_agg = 0.75 in</expbody><expresult> = 0.750 in</expresult></dynexp><break type="tab"/>Assumed nominal maximum aggregate size for detailing.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_face = A_grid*(12 in)/s_grid to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_face = A_grid*(12 in)/s_grid to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.660 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Distributed steel provided per foot, each face and each direction.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_ST_raw = 1.30*(H_w/(1 in))*(t_w/(1 in))/(2*(H_w/(1 in)+t_w/(1 in))*(f_y/(1 ksi)))*(1 in^2) to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_ST_raw = 1.30*(H_w/(1 in))*(t_w/(1 in))/(2*(H_w/(1 in)+t_w/(1 in))*(f_y/(1 ksi)))*(1 in^2) to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.323 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Shrinkage/temperature requirement for a one-foot strip on each face. (LRFD Eq. 5.10.6-1) (LRFD Eq. 5.10.6-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_ST_other = 1.30*(L_w/(1 in))*(t_w/(1 in))/(2*(L_w/(1 in)+t_w/(1 in))*(f_y/(1 ksi)))*(1 in^2) to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_ST_other = 1.30*(L_w/(1 in))*(t_w/(1 in))/(2*(L_w/(1 in)+t_w/(1 in))*(f_y/(1 ksi)))*(1 in^2) to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.334 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Other full-component section for distributed reinforcement. (LRFD Eq. 5.10.6-1) (LRFD Eq. 5.10.6-1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="A_ST = Min(0.60 in^2,Max(0.11 in^2,A_ST_raw,A_ST_other)) to in^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>A_ST = Min(0.60 in^2,Max(0.11 in^2,A_ST_raw,A_ST_other)) to in^2</expbody><expresult> = 0.334 in^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Required shrinkage/temperature area per one-foot strip. (LRFD Eq. 5.10.6-2) (LRFD Eq. 5.10.6-2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="ρ_grid = 2*A_grid/(t_w*s_grid)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>ρ_grid = 2*A_grid/(t_w*s_grid)</expbody><expresult> = 0.003</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Total two-face reinforcement ratio in each direction.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_ST = If(t_w&gt;18 in,12 in,Max(3*t_w,18 in)) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_ST = If(t_w&gt;18 in,12 in,Max(3*t_w,18 in)) to in</expbody><expresult> = 12.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Shrinkage/temperature maximum spacing. (LRFD 5.10.6) (LRFD 5.10.6)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_general = Min(1.5*t_w,18 in) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_general = Min(1.5*t_w,18 in) to in</expbody><expresult> = 18.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">General wall/slab maximum bar spacing. (LRFD 5.10.3.2) (LRFD 5.10.3.2)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_clear_req = Max(1.5*d_grid,1.5*a_agg,1.5 in) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_clear_req = Max(1.5*d_grid,1.5*a_agg,1.5 in) to in</expbody><expresult> = 1.500 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Minimum clear spacing within the wall grid. (LRFD 5.10.3.1.1) (LRFD 5.10.3.1.1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="s_clear = s_grid-d_grid to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>s_clear = s_grid-d_grid to in</expbody><expresult> = 7.250 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Provided clear spacing of parallel grid bars.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="g_pipe = t_w/2-D_p/2-T_pos-c_w-2*d_grid to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>g_pipe = t_w/2-D_p/2-T_pos-c_w-2*d_grid to in</expbody><expresult> = 1.500 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Conservative gap from shifted pipe to innermost face-grid surface.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="g_fins = S_p-D_p-2*a_p to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>g_fins = S_p-D_p-2*a_p to in</expbody><expresult> = 24.000 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Clear tip-to-tip distance for opposed fins in a pile bay.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="l_db_grid = 0.17*d_grid*((f_y/(1 ksi))/(1.97*Sqrt(Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi)))))^2 to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>l_db_grid = 0.17*d_grid*((f_y/(1 ksi))/(1.97*Sqrt(Sqrt(f_c/(1 ksi)))))^2 to in</expbody><expresult> = 50.431 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Basic full-yield straight development of a #6 grid bar. (LRFD Eq. 5.10.8.2.1a-2) (LRFD Eq. 5.10.8.2.1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="l_d_grid = Max(12 in,1.3*l_db_grid) to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>l_d_grid = Max(12 in,1.3*l_db_grid) to in</expbody><expresult> = 65.560 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Horizontal top-cast grid development; no confinement reduction. (LRFD 5.10.8.2.1a-b) (LRFD 5.10.8.2.1)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="l_lap = 1.3*l_d_grid to in" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>l_lap = 1.3*l_d_grid to in</expbody><expresult> = 85.229 in</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Selected conservative Class B tension-lap length. (LRFD 5.10.8.4.3) (LRFD 5.10.8.4.3)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="V_conc = L_w*t_w*H_w to ft^3" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>V_conc = L_w*t_w*H_w to ft^3</expbody><expresult> = 764.914 ft^3</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Gross concrete volume for mass-concrete screening.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="S_conc = 2*(L_w*t_w+L_w*H_w+t_w*H_w) to ft^2" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>S_conc = 2*(L_w*t_w+L_w*H_w+t_w*H_w) to ft^2</expbody><expresult> = 702.630 ft^2</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">All six gross exterior faces for mass-concrete screening.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="R_VS = V_conc/S_conc to ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>R_VS = V_conc/S_conc to ft</expbody><expresult> = 1.089 ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Volume-to-surface-area ratio.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Status_mass = If(And(Min(L_w,t_w,H_w)&gt;3 ft,R_VS&gt;1 ft),&quot;MASS CONCRETE — thermal controls required&quot;,&quot;Not triggered by SDG dimensional screen&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Status_mass = If(And(Min(L_w,t_w,H_w)&gt;3 ft,R_VS&gt;1 ft),"MASS CONCRETE — thermal controls required","Not triggered by SDG dimensional screen")</expbody><expresult> = Not triggered by SDG dimensional screen</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">FDOT mass-concrete dimensional screen. (FDOT SDG 1.4.4) (SDG 1.4.4)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_ST = If(And(A_face&gt;=A_ST,s_grid&lt;=s_ST,s_grid&lt;=s_general), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_ST = If(And(A_face&gt;=A_ST,s_grid&lt;=s_ST,s_grid&lt;=s_general), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Shrinkage/temperature steel and maximum spacing, both directions and faces.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_STMgrid = If(And(ρ_grid&gt;=ρ_STM,s_grid&lt;=12 in), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_STMgrid = If(And(ρ_grid&gt;=ρ_STM,s_grid&lt;=12 in), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Adopted disturbed-region grid area and twelve-inch ceiling. (LRFD 5.8.2.6) (LRFD 5.8.2.6)</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#A64A20">The additional d/4 spacing condition in LRFD 5.8.2.6 must be checked against the actual local strut-and-tie model. The twelve-inch ceiling and area ratio above do not alone close that local model.</paragraph> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_spacing = If(And(s_clear&gt;=s_clear_req,s_tie&lt;=12 in), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_spacing = If(And(s_clear&gt;=s_clear_req,s_tie&lt;=12 in), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">General grid clear spacing and selected cross-tie spacing.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_fit = If(And(g_pipe&gt;=g_place,c_pipe_end&gt;=c_w,g_fins&gt;0 in), &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_fit = If(And(g_pipe&gt;=g_place,c_pipe_end&gt;=c_w,g_fins&gt;0 in), "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Selected trial layout fits only within the specified pile-position envelope.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Chk_joints = If(L_w&lt;=30 ft, &quot;✓ PASS&quot;, &quot;⊗ FAIL&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Chk_joints = If(L_w&lt;=30 ft, "✓ PASS", "⊗ FAIL")</expbody><expresult> = ✓ PASS</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall length does not require an intermediate joint under the 30-foot screen. (FDOT SDG 3.10.C) (SDG 3.10.C)</paragraph><table name="C006Box238" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A7" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box238R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">REINFORCEMENT AND CONSTRUCTION NOTES</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box238R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Provide the selected face grid in both directions at each broad face, with horizontal bars outermost. Continue the face grids around ends and edges using developed returns or compatible laps; do not cut bars off merely because they meet a pipe.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box238R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Provide the selected through-thickness cross-ties at the spacing shown above, positively engaging the outer horizontal bars at both faces with compliant hooks. Verify the actual tie configuration under LRFD 5.10.8.2.6.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box238R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Provide two designated #5 hairpins at every fin; no credit from the distributed grid is included in the fin-development target. Additional local concrete splitting/strut reinforcement is subject to the local node design.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box238R4" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Drive and survey piles before fabricating/installing final fins and reinforcement. The selected wall fit requires the position envelope shown above, including the transverse direction; the current cap tolerance cannot be substituted unchecked.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box238R5" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Forms/falsework carry wet concrete until the concrete and anchorage have the required strength. The completed embedded bearing mechanism is not assumed available in fresh concrete.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box238R6" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">No collision or seismic exemption is newly certified here. Retain the established project applicability decisions only after confirming the governing geometry and classification. Construction, fatigue, and differential-pile-movement effects outside the assigned loads remain coordination items.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <section name="C006Work07" capture="False" hide="false"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="6" fontweight="bold" textcolor="#1766A0" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" id="c006work07">Step 7. Weld and pile interface actions</paragraph></section><table name="C006Box240" capture="False" colwidths="1:650">
                <stylerule range="A1:A6" background="#F1F5FA" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#7189A6&quot;);"/>
                <stylerule range="A1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box240R0" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">LOCAL WELD HANDOFF AXES AND REFERENCE</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box240R1" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">O is the midheight of the nominal full-height fin root at the pipe tangent plane. Local +x points outward along that fin, +z points downward, and +y is chosen so x cross y = z (right-handed).</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box240R2" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Fz is positive downward. A downward load at positive x creates negative My. A positive transverse offset creates positive Mx. Reversing the transverse offset reverses Mx; the paired rows below are complete concurrent cases.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box240R3" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">For opposite-facing fins, the local axes rotate with the fin. Transform each complete case to the weld program axes. If the actual weld-group centroid differs from O, relocate once using Mnew = Mold + r cross F.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box240R4" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Fx, Fy and Mz are zero in the assigned vertical hanger model, not measured zero compatibility actions. Wall-wind reactions enter the piles through the separate distributed contact path. Any force assigned to the fin by a revised model must be added as a complete load case.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
                <row>
                    <textcell name="C006Box240R5" capture="False"> <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Actual Service I and Strength I/III rows are load demands. HY+ and HY- are nominal-hairpin-yield development targets and must not be multiplied by the DC or wind factors again. They are not asserted to occur simultaneously at every fin.</paragraph> </textcell> </row>
            </table>
  <section name="step_7_weld_and_pile_interface_actionsRows" capture="False" hide="true"><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Working rows (hidden): the row-by-row definitions behind the tables.</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Fz_SI_F1 = R_1+W_a to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Fz_SI_F1 = R_1+W_a to kip</expbody><expresult> = 33.303 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Fz_SI_F1</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="My_SI_F1 = -(R_1*e_actual+W_p*a_p/2+W_s*e_h) to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>My_SI_F1 = -(R_1*e_actual+W_p*a_p/2+W_s*e_h) to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = -10.684 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">My_SI_F1</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Mx_SI_F1 = R_1*e_y to kip*ft" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Mx_SI_F1 = R_1*e_y to kip*ft</expbody><expresult> = 0.693 kip*ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Mx_SI_F1</paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="4" keepwithnext="True"><dynexp formula="Fz_U_F1 = γ_DC*(R_1+W_a) to kip" mathlayout="on" showformula="True" showresult="True" showsteps="False"><expbody>Fz_U_F1 = γ_DC*(R_1+W_a) to kip</expbody><expresult> = 41.628 kip</expresult></dynexp></paragraph><paragraph fontfamily="Ti